      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`test/registered/kv_canary/test_self_e2e_canary_info.py` has failed on main since #41916, which makes the scheduler abort any request with `min_p > 0` on a speculative-decoding server ([scheduled run job](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41736410757/job/126266970572)).\n\nThe test's servers run EAGLE, and 2 of its 8 requests (`canary-info-2`, `canary-info-6`) used `min_p=0.05` from `CANARY_INFO_SAMPLING_PARAMS`. Both were aborted (`min_p is not supported with EAGLE speculative decoding`), and the test expects every request to finish with `length`.\n\n## Modifications\n\nDrop `min_p` from that entry, keeping `temperature=1.0, top_k=20`. `CANARY_INFO_SAMPLING_PARAMS` is only used by the canary-info e2e tests, all of which run EAGLE. The unit test `test_self_unit_canary_info.py` still covers `min_p` in the sampling digest.\n\n## Notes\n\nIn the failing run, the aborted `canary-info-2` also reported a first output token whose canary info didn't match, and with `--kv-canary raise` that crashed the server (exit 137), cutting off every other stream. That is a separate question for the canary hook (should aborted requests be checked?) and is not changed here.\n\ncc @alvion427 @Qiaolin-Yu\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] `/rerun-test test/registered/kv_canary/test_self_e2e_canary_info.py`\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41795645220](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41795645220)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41795645064](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41795645064)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41795645010](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41795645010)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
